     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose the risk of severe GI effects and lactic acidosis goes up, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, divided into a different schedule\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intended, tell me and add a note about your rationale. I'd still suggest confirming it first."
      }
     ],
